# Every text file in this repository is UTF-8 with LF endings, on every platform
# and whatever a machine's global `core.autocrlf` happens to be. Without this,
# checking out on Windows rewrites every line ending on the way in and each commit
# prints a warning about the ones it is about to change. The warnings are noise,
# and noise is how a real one gets missed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never convert these: a line-ending pass over a font or an icon corrupts it.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.db binary

# Keep the licence texts byte-exact. They are quoted by other projects and by
# package registries, and a rewritten line ending is a different file.
LICENSE-MIT -text
LICENSE-APACHE -text

# A source listing that Git counts wrong is a listing that looks like a merge
# conflict in review. These are the generated or vendored ones, marked so they do
# not appear in language statistics.
Cargo.lock linguist-generated
app/package-lock.json linguist-generated